+// Credits are EXACT per receiver: receiver `rank` increments its own word (cb_x_credits + rank) on every injector, and
+// an injector sends round k only once EVERY word is >= k + 1. (Round 1 summed all credits on one semaphore: with credits
+// more than one round ahead a fast receiver's extra credits stood in for a slow receiver's missing one, and the
+// injector overwrote a slot the slow receiver still held -- the ~1 in 8 corrupted chip-calls.) The injector zeroes its
+// words, then arms every receiver (sem_x_armed += 1); a receiver credits only once all NI injectors armed it.
+// x_credit_slots (default): instead of the words, one credit counter PER SLOT on each injector (sem_x_slot + a %
+// depth); the injector sends round k once counter k % depth >= C1 * (k / depth + 1). Sound for any lead: a receiver
+// can credit lap L + 1 of a slot only after popping round k (lap L), i.e. after round k was sent, so before that send
+// every receiver's count on the slot is <= L + 1 and the sum reaching C1 * (L + 1) means each one is exactly L + 1.
+// One semaphore wait per round on the injector (the words cost a C1-word scan per round).
+// X_SPLIT (s1_pace, from round-1 x_supply): each of the NI injectors multicasts ITS tile range of EVERY round (one
+// tree per NoC, both busy every round) and publishes the count of rounds it has sent on its own ready counter
+// (sem_x_ready + i, a plain multicast write behind the linked payload). The counter is monotone and never cleared, so
+// a receiver credits slots up to `ahead` rounds ahead (to every injector: each sends part of every round) without a
+// per-round credit round trip. One credit state across the q_b pre-delivery and the main loop.
+// Raw (no Mcast helper): the helper's Flag allows one outstanding round per family, its Counter costs a write +
+// atomic barrier per round.
+template <uint32_t NI>
+struct XSplitRx {
+    uint32_t cb, round_tiles, num_rounds, ahead, sem_ready;
+    const uint64_t* inj_credit;
+    uint32_t sem_armed;
+    bool slots;                 // per-slot counters (inj_credit = the injectors' semaphore-0 base NoC address)
+    uint32_t sem_slot, depth;  // slot s counter = semaphore sem_slot + s on the injector
+    uint32_t acked = 0;  // rounds credited so far (to every injector)
+    bool armed = false;
+    // credit every round in [acked, r + ahead) whose slot is free; block for slot r itself (polling `idle`)
+    template <typename I>
+    void credit(uint32_t r, I&& idle) {
+        while (acked < num_rounds && acked < r + ahead) {
+            const uint32_t pages = (acked - r + 1) * round_tiles;  // slots r .. acked free
